{
  "note": "Tuning set, writer A. Written to fit the router's cut-offs; it is not evidence of accuracy. Labels follow the policy below.",
  "policy": "TOOLSETS (multi-label; a message gets EVERY toolset its job needs, possibly none):\n- calendar: the owner's own Google Calendar — events, classes/lectures, meetings, schedule, free time, creating/moving/deleting events, answering invites, \"what's next\", \"my day\".\n- maps: places and getting around — a place's address or Google Maps link, directions, travel time, routes, traffic, places nearby (cafés, restaurants to visit), weather/forecast.\n- gmail: the owner's own email — finding, reading, counting mail; what someone sent; receipts in mail. (Read only.)\n- drive: the owner's Google Drive — finding/reading a doc, sheet, slides, PDF stored there; creating a doc there.\n- github: the owner's GitHub — repos, issues, PRs, commits, branches, CI/build status.\n- doordash: ordering food, groceries or retail delivery/pickup through DoorDash — finding what's open to order, menus, carts, placing/reordering/tracking an order, past orders.\n- share: sending a file from the owner's Mac TO ANOTHER PERSON by iMessage or email (\"send the deck to Ana\"). Sending a file to the owner themself in this chat is NOT share.\n- workspace: the owner's Slack, Notion or Linear (messages, channels, pages, tickets).\nNot a toolset (label none of the above for these): general chat, web facts/news/opening hours of a business from the web, math, coding questions, memory (\"what did I say about…\"), controlling the Mac screen (\"close my tabs\"), lights/TV/music, reminders the assistant keeps itself, sending a file to the owner themself.\nCompound jobs get several labels (\"my next class and a maps link\" -> calendar+maps; \"email Ana the PDF from my drive\" -> drive+share; \"order lunch to my 2pm meeting's room\" -> doordash+calendar).",
